questions.explanation:
Each term is obtained by multiplying the preceding term by -2 (geometric progression with common ratio q = -2):
5 × (-2) = -10;
-10 × (-2) = +20;
20 × (-2) = -40;
-40 × (-2) = +80;
80 × (-2) = -160;
-160 × (-2) = +320.
Option C is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Geometrische Folge mit dem Quotienten q = -2:
5  (-2) = -10;
-10  (-2) = 20;
20  (-2) = -40;
-40  (-2) = 80;
80  (-2) = -160;
-160  (-2) = +320.
Option C ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
Each term is divided by -3 (or multiplied by -1/3):
486 ÷ (-3) = -162;
-162 ÷ (-3) = +54;
54 ÷ (-3) = -18;
-18 ÷ (-3) = +6;
+6 ÷ (-3) = -2.
Option D is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Jedes Folgenglied wird durch -3 dividiert:
486 : (-3) = -162;
-162 : (-3) = 54;
54 : (-3) = -18;
-18 : (-3) = 6;
6 : (-3) = -2.
Option D ist richtig.

Jedes Folgenglied wird mit -3 multipliziert:
-2  (-3) = 6;
6  (-3) = -18;
-18  (-3) = 54;
54  (-3) = -162;
-162  (-3) = +486.
Option A ist richtig.

Jedes Folgenglied wird mit -4 multipliziert:
1  (-4) = -4;
-4  (-4) = 16;
16  (-4) = -64;
-64  (-4) = 256;
256  (-4) = -1024.
Option C ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
This is a Fibonacci-type recurrence where each term (starting from the 3rd) is the sum of the preceding two terms:
4 + 6 = 10;
6 + 10 = 16;
10 + 16 = 26;
16 + 26 = 42;
26 + 42 = 68.
Option D is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Fibonacci-artige Rekursion (Summe der beiden vorangehenden Glieder):
4 + 6 = 10;
6 + 10 = 16;
10 + 16 = 26;
16 + 26 = 42;
26 + 42 = 68.
Option D ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
Each term from the third onwards is the sum of the previous two terms:
1 + 4 = 5;
4 + 5 = 9;
5 + 9 = 14;
9 + 14 = 23;
14 + 23 = 37;
23 + 37 = 60.
Option A is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Jedes Glied ab dem dritten ist die Summe der beiden Vorgänger:
1 + 4 = 5;
4 + 5 = 9;
5 + 9 = 14;
9 + 14 = 23;
14 + 23 = 37;
23 + 37 = 60.
Option A ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
This recurrence satisfies x_n = 2 × x_{n-1} + x_{n-2} (Pell sequence):
2 × 2 + 1 = 5;
2 × 5 + 2 = 12;
2 × 12 + 5 = 29;
2 × 29 + 12 = 70;
2 × 70 + 29 = 140 + 29 = 169.
Option B is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Pell-Zahlenfolge mit der Rekursionsformel x_n = 2  x_{n-1} + x_{n-2}:
2  2 + 1 = 5;
2  5 + 2 = 12;
2  12 + 5 = 29;
2  29 + 12 = 70;
2  70 + 29 = 140 + 29 = 169.
Option B ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
This is the Tribonacci sequence, where each term (starting from the 4th) is the sum of the preceding three terms:
1 + 1 + 2 = 4;
1 + 2 + 4 = 7;
2 + 4 + 7 = 13;
4 + 7 + 13 = 24;
7 + 13 + 24 = 44.
Option C is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Tribonacci-Folge: Jedes Glied ab dem 4. ist die Summe der drei vorhergehenden Glieder:
1 + 1 + 2 = 4;
1 + 2 + 4 = 7;
2 + 4 + 7 = 13;
4 + 7 + 13 = 24;
7 + 13 + 24 = 44.
Option C ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
Examine the recurrence: each term is the sum of the previous two terms minus 2:
3 + 5 - 2 = 6;
5 + 6 - 2 = 9;
6 + 9 - 2 = 13;
9 + 13 - 2 = 20;
13 + 20 - 2 = 31.
Option D is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Rekursionsmuster: Jedes Glied ist die Summe der vorherigen zwei Glieder abzüglich 2:
3 + 5 - 2 = 6;
5 + 6 - 2 = 9;
6 + 9 - 2 = 13;
9 + 13 - 2 = 20;
13 + 20 - 2 = 31.
Option D ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
Adding 1 to each term reveals the sequence of consecutive prime numbers:
1 + 1 = 2;
2 + 1 = 3;
4 + 1 = 5;
6 + 1 = 7;
10 + 1 = 11;
12 + 1 = 13;
16 + 1 = 17.
The next prime number is 19. Therefore, the next term is 19 - 1 = 18. Option B is correct.

Compare each term to perfect cubes (n^3 - 2):
2^3 - 2 = 8 - 2 = 6;
3^3 - 2 = 27 - 2 = 25;
4^3 - 2 = 64 - 2 = 62;
5^3 - 2 = 125 - 2 = 123;
6^3 - 2 = 216 - 2 = 214.
The next term corresponds to n = 7: 7^3 - 2 = 343 - 2 = 341. Option C is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Kubikzahlen minus 2 (n³ - 2):
2³ - 2 = 6;
3³ - 2 = 25;
4³ - 2 = 62;
5³ - 2 = 123;
6³ - 2 = 214.
Das nächste Glied für n = 7 ist 7³ - 2 = 343 - 2 = 341. Option C ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
These are perfect squares plus 3 (n^2 + 3):
1^2 + 3 = 4;
2^2 + 3 = 7;
3^2 + 3 = 12;
4^2 + 3 = 19;
5^2 + 3 = 28;
6^2 + 3 = 39.
The next term is 7^2 + 3 = 49 + 3 = 52. (Alternatively, differences increase by odd numbers: +3, +5, +7, +9, +11, next is +13 -> 39 + 13 = 52). Option D is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Quadratzahlen plus 3 (n² + 3):
1² + 3 = 4;
2² + 3 = 7;
3² + 3 = 12;
4² + 3 = 19;
5² + 3 = 28;
6² + 3 = 39.
Nächstes Glied: 7² + 3 = 49 + 3 = 52 (oder Differenzen +3, +5, +7, +9, +11, +13: 39 + 13 = 52). Option D ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
Compare each term to perfect cubes n^3:
1^3 - 1 = 0;
2^3 + 1 = 9;
3^3 - 1 = 26;
4^3 + 1 = 65;
5^3 - 1 = 124.
The formula is n^3 + (-1)^n (alternating -1, +1, -1, +1, -1). For n = 6 (even), we add 1:
6^3 + 1 = 216 + 1 = 217. Option A is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Kubikzahlen mit alternierendem Offset: n³ + (-1)^n (abwechselnd -1, +1):
1³ - 1 = 0;
2³ + 1 = 9;
3³ - 1 = 26;
4³ + 1 = 65;
5³ - 1 = 124.
Für n = 6 (gerade Zahl) lautet die Operation +1: 6³ + 1 = 216 + 1 = 217. Option A ist richtig.

questions.explanation:
These are perfect cubes plus 2 (n^3 + 2):
1^3 + 2 = 3;
2^3 + 2 = 10;
3^3 + 2 = 29;
4^3 + 2 = 66;
5^3 + 2 = 127.
The next term for n = 6 is 6^3 + 2 = 216 + 2 = 218. Option B is correct.

questions.explanation_de:
Kubikzahlen plus 2 (n³ + 2):
1³ + 2 = 3;
2³ + 2 = 10;
3³ + 2 = 29;
4³ + 2 = 66;
5³ + 2 = 127.
Nächstes Glied für n = 6: 6³ + 2 = 216 + 2 = 218. Option B ist richtig.
